{"availability":"available","full":"fazal305/formforge","name":"formforge","description":"Design a form visually. Generate the application behind it. Schema-driven form builder with HTML/CSS/JS, PHP, and MySQL code generation.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-18T05:37:44Z","updated":"2026-10-08T06:11:57Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://formforge-ochre.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://formforge-ochre.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.541Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.541Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.541Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.541Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Design a form visually. Generate the application behind it.","FormForge is a schema-driven visual form builder and code generator. You design a form on a canvas — drag or click to add fields, configure validation, preview it live — and FormForge compiles that design into a standalone, independent project: a real HTML/CSS/JS frontend, a PHP backend with server-side validation and secure file uploads, and a MySQL schema, all downloadable as a ZIP.","It isn't a form-with-a-submit-button. The architecture is closer to a small compiler: one internal Form Schema feeds every output (preview, HTML, JavaScript, PHP, SQL, JSON Schema), so nothing is hand-authored twice and nothing can silently drift out of sync."],"features":["Visual builder — click-to-add or drag-and-drop fields (accessible keyboard reordering via dnd-kit), 14 field types, undo/redo, a generic properties panel driven entirely by each field type's own registry entry (no…","Live preview — a real interactive rendering of the schema, running the same validation rules the export will use, with a submission simulation (success/error states)","Code generation — HTML, CSS, vanilla JavaScript, JSON Schema, a PHP REST backend, and MySQL CREATE TABLE SQL, each an independent, pure generator function","Security by construction — every generated file escapes schema data appropriately for its target (HTML entities, JSON.stringify, a custom PHP literal encoder); server-side validation never trusts the client; file…","Code viewer — syntax-highlighted, copy/download per file, plus a Database Designer table showing the field→column mapping before you commit to it"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fazal305/formforge/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"ba019f10ae1be824de0d9a8016b5b1946e68def064ac8379697f5af134e3e6ed","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.709Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.709Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Design a form visually. Generate the application behind it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fazal305/formforge/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"Local-first — no account, no backend of its own; your form design autosaves to your browser and can be saved, exported as JSON, or imported back in","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fazal305/formforge/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"ba019f10ae1be824de0d9a8016b5b1946e68def064ac8379697f5af134e3e6ed","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fazal305/formforge/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.710Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T06:11:57Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fazal305/formforge/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.710Z","hash":"ba019f10ae1be824de0d9a8016b5b1946e68def064ac8379697f5af134e3e6ed","originalBytes":7983,"storedBytes":7983,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["schema","php","form","export","validation","field","backend","generated","html","never","code","every","file","json","design","formforge","preview","builder","fields","generators","live","sql","css","database","each","generator","independent","npm","real","application","generation",